title: The Eight-Hour Day
subtitle: The southern metalworkers strike against a longer week.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1922 and month = 5
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
RG.news('Lenin taken ill at Gorki', 2);
Q.e22_metal_ok = 0;
!}

= The Eight-Hour Day

The metal employers of Württemberg and Bavaria want forty-eight hours a week instead of forty-six, for the same wage. Since March tens of thousands of men have been on strike or locked out. The union's strike fund is empty and the employers say they will starve them back.

The eight-hour day was the one gain of November 1918 that every worker feels in his legs. [? if bavaria_soviet = 2 : In Red Bavaria the councils decreed it long ago, and the employers in Stuttgart point to Munich as a warning. ?]

- @collect: Take collections for the strike fund.
- @occupy: Tell the locked-out men to occupy the works.
- @may_day: Make May Day their day.

@collect
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. A gesture the south will remember.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have nothing to send.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
RG.district('bavaria', {members: 0.08, loyalty: 6});
Q.e22_metal = 2;
!}

Collection lists go round the Berlin and Saxon works. The money is small. In Stuttgart and Munich they know where it came from.

@occupy
subtitle: [? if lock_councils = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Walcher thinks they might hold the works one time in three. If they do, the employers give way.
choose-if: lock_councils < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids occupations.
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.against('councils');
Q.e22_metal = 3;
Q.e22_metal_ok = Math.random() < 0.35 ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.e22_metal_ok) {
    RG.district('bavaria', {members: 0.15, loyalty: 10, militancy: 8});
    Q.worker_support += 4;
    RG.ledger('The occupied metal works of the south saved the forty-six-hour week.', 'e22_metal');
} else {
    RG.district('bavaria', {members: -0.1, repression: 10});
}
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

[? if e22_metal_ok = 1 : The men of Bosch in Stuttgart and MAN in Augsburg hold their works for eleven days. On the twelfth the employers' association withdraws its demand. ?][? if e22_metal_ok = 0 : The Württemberg police clear the works on the third day. Our men are the first on the employers' blacklists. ?]

@may_day
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] One slogan in every procession, beside the unions.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids marching with the reformist unions.
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.against('united_front');
Q.e22_metal = 1;
Q.worker_support += 3;
Q.spd_relation += 3;
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
!}

On May Day the slogan is the same in every procession: hands off the eight-hour day. The strike ends in late May with a compromise that keeps the principle.
